Nano-to-Macro Transport Processes — MIT 2.57 (@th-nano: 0, is #reference, #part-of @th-sources) { r_1YF7TD689ZRGQ51D4B3NGVHZQG
Gang Chen. MIT 2.57, Spring 2012, graduate. [Complete public course](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/2-57-nano-to-macro-transport-processes-spring-2012/) · [Lecture-note provenance](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/2-57-nano-to-macro-transport-processes-spring-2012/pages/lecture-notes/).

Study the full available lecture/video, homework, examination and project progression after the continuum foundation. Develop microscopic carriers, dispersion, distributions, transport equations and the approximations connecting them to macroscopic energy transport. Follow the actual mathematics, including the quantum/statistical preparation used in each derivation.

The downloadable complete notes are from Fall 2004 and serve as a reference for Spring 2012; they are not newly written 2012 notes. Public lectures and notes do not confer access to the separately published commercial textbook. OCW's CC BY-NC-SA terms and component exceptions apply. No source course, code or media is copied into the repository.

**Return:** [Thermodynamics and heat transfer sources](../Sources.lingua#r_4N96T70VYW3C3M91M2SXF5KEQF).
